===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|ram|lang=gmh}}, {{term|rame||column, frame|lang=gmh|g=f}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|rama||support|lang=goh|g=f}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*ramō||prop, frame}}, probably from  {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*rem(w)-||to rest, prop up; a support, base}}. Cognate with {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|rame|rāme|lang=gml|g=m}}, {{etyl|dum|-}} {{term|rame|rāme|lang=dum|g=m}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|raam|lang=nl|g=n}}. Related to {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|Rand||edge|lang=de|g=m}} and {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|Ranft||crust of bread|lang=de|g=m}} (see also {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|Kanten|lang=de}}), {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|ramft|lang=goh}}, {{etyl|gmh|-}} {{term|ranft|lang=gmh}}, {{term|ramft||edge, edging|lang=gmh}}, {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐍂𐌹𐌼𐌹𐍃||silence}}, {{etyl|sa|-}} {{m|sa|रमते||he sets at rest|tr=rámate}}, {{m|sa|रम्भ||prop, staff, support|tr=rambhá}}.

